{
  "$comment": "Page contracts, version 3 (docs/design/target-state.md v2.1). One entry per surface the UI inventory walks. Every rendered heading, tab, tile, column, chip, button, summary and link on a built surface must match an entry in its allow list (exact string, or a regular expression when prefixed re:). Page-level prose (outside repeaters) must fit the budget. Claude Code never edits this file: a violation is fixed by removing what violates it, or reported for review with the case. `status` is `built` for a surface that is measured; a status of the form `planned:<prompt>` names the prompt that builds the surface and flips it to `built` — a surface that is not `built` is not measured. `enforceAll` is true: any inventory surface without a contract fails, so a deleted surface (the Recovery card) fails the build if it still renders. Controls (buttons, links, chips) inside a repeater are items and are measured under `rows`, not against the surface's allow lists. An element matching `.step-title` is reported as `title` and measured against rules.stepTitleMaxWords, never as a heading. A surface may override the row budget with `rowBudget`. `forbid` and `forbidEverywhere` entries are case-sensitive substrings.",
